## T-11 — pure-function regression (see baseline-03.log for why this
## couldn't be exercised against a real Env either before or after)

$ cargo test -p noye-gateway env_check::tests
test env_check::tests::leaked_value_is_refused ... ok
test env_check::tests::leaked_value_is_refused_with_no_development_bypass ... ok
test env_check::tests::non_denylisted_value_is_accepted ... ok
test env_check::tests::unset_variable_is_accepted ... ok
test env_check::tests::no_observations_at_all_is_accepted ... ok
test env_check::tests::error_names_the_variable_but_not_the_value ... ok
test env_check::tests::only_the_leaked_variable_is_named_when_only_one_leaks ... ok
6 passed

$ cargo test -p noye-core env_check::tests
test env_check::tests::leaked_value_is_refused_with_no_development_bypass ... ok
test env_check::tests::non_denylisted_value_is_accepted ... ok
test env_check::tests::unset_variable_is_accepted ... ok
test env_check::tests::error_names_the_variable_but_not_the_value ... ok
5 passed

`find_leaked_fallback` takes no environment/is-development parameter at
all in either crate — there is no branch left that could reintroduce
the pre-fix bypass. This is a structural argument, same class as T-06/
T-07 in Subject 02: the property is verified by the function's type
signature and a passing test suite, not by exercising a live Workers
`Env` with `NOYE_ENV=development` set, which remains impossible here.

## T-12, T-13, T-14 — not independently exercised

Guards, per the subject's own Verify table. T-12 (refused when
production) and T-13 (refused when unset) hold by the same
no-environment-parameter argument as T-11 — the function does not
distinguish the three cases at all, so there is exactly one code path
for all of them, already tested above. T-14 (Gateway → Core auth with a
generated token) requires two live Workers talking to each other and
was not exercised.

## T-15 — refusal message names the variable, not the value

Directly tested: `error_names_the_variable_but_not_the_value` in both
crates (above).
